single-flight refresh (p1-s6), but THIS prompt is scoped to apps/apple/** only — so the
Apple-native auth stack is implemented in Swift and exposes seams the facade hands to KMP
networking. Reused design-system components (TSButton/TSEmptyState/TSAlertBanner/TSSpinner/
TSPageLoader) + tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius) + AppShell/AppRoute.

=== REASONING / ARCHITECTURE ===
- To maximize host-verified coverage, the ENTIRE auth stack lives in Sources/Auth/** with
  NO `import Shared` → fully host-typechecked. The facade hand-off is a thin, minimal seam
  on AppContainer (deferred bucket).
- Crypto/flow is pure Foundation/Security/CryptoKit/LocalAuthentication/AuthenticationServices.
  PKCE is S256-only (RFC 7636); verifier/state/nonce from SecRandomCopyBytes; challenge =
  base64url(SHA256(verifier)).
- Tokens persist ONLY in Keychain (generic-password, access-group capable, AfterFirstUnlock-
  ThisDeviceOnly default, optional biometric SecAccessControl). Never UserDefaults/files/logs.
  Only the biometric on/off *flag* is in UserDefaults.
- AuthCoordinator is @MainActor @Observable. Refresh is single-flight (concurrent 401s await
  one in-flight Task). Failed refresh clears secrets and routes to reauth. It conforms to
  AuthTokenProviding (bearer header) + AuthChallengeHandling (centralized 401), and exposes
  authStateStream() as the SSE re-auth seam.
- RootView is the onboarding gate: one real surface per state (splash / onboarding+sign-in /
  biometric unlock / reauth / AppShell + expiring banner + reauth overlay). No blank screens.
- Logging goes through AuthLog, which redacts tokens, VINs, and precise coordinates (ADR-016).

